Z||000000||bHooper||01-11-2001||04:44 PM||||ever now and then, when i crank the car to go somewhere (and it's cold out), i notice some moisture build up on the inside right rear qtr window and right side of the rear window.<P>i never notice this at any other time, except at cold start/crank.<P>anyone have a clue as to where this is coming from?<P>thanks!<P>hoop<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-11-2001||07:43 PM||||could be an exhaust leak or just exhaust blowing back under the car and comming up thru the grate. Hard to say without seeing it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||01-11-2001||08:38 PM||||exaust leaks are a plenty on this car... sounds like a harley coming at ya!<P>i really don't want to do anything to the exhaust, because i'm cheap and plan on doing the 3.4l sometime next year.<P>but i may have no choice.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||01-11-2001||11:48 PM||||as your car begins to heat up warmer than the ambient temperature it will dissipate out of the right vent due to the rotation of the water  pump/alternator/air conditioning units - this strikes the corner inside the rear window and quarter window and will fog it up in a hurry - it happens to most of us -- the conditions have to be right though - too hot or too cold and this phenomonen won't occur.........mine did it tonight........<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
